From f9d2d85fa57b24443a061338b79a7e7379ce353f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: evilcomputer12 <martinrobotika@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:55:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/8] xodus: Add relying-party resolution and Xbox Live request
 signing.

resolve_relying_party() picks the relying party and signature policy for a
request URL from the title.mgt endpoint table the way XUserGetTokenAndSignature
does (protocol + fqdn/wildcard host + optional exact path, most specific entry
wins, http://xboxlive.com as the default). TitleMgtEndPoint now carries Path.

signing::sign_request() produces the Signature header value (ES256 over policy
version, FILETIME, method, path+query, Authorization and the body prefix) with
a p256 proof key, reusing xal's prehash layout. It exists so the service can
sign a request that the game, not the service, is going to send; the test
checks the result byte-for-byte against xal's RequestSigner.

xsts_user_only() is a non-panicking version of api::xbox::run().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
